  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5057",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the interaction with CGTH-W-1 through a multi-step pathway involving purinoceptor and secondary metabolite targets. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin acts as a target for P2X purinoceptor 1 and Mollicellin N, both of which in turn target CGTH-W-1. This indicates a potential mechanism where doxorubicin may influence cellular processes through these intermediaries. The presence of multiple pathways with similar scores suggests a consistent relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The integration of these targets highlights the complexity of the molecular network, emphasizing the role of purinoceptors and secondary metabolites in mediating drug effects.",
